  "body": "Closes #7491:\n\n> The description references three groups of headers:\n> - The headers in the first row\n> - The headers with the explicit scope attributes\n> - The remaining headers\n>\n> But since in the example HTML *all* of the headers beyond the first row have explicit scope, the second and third groups are identical and the description becomes incorrect.  \n>\n> https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#the-th-element\n>\n> > The following example shows how the scope attribute's rowgroup value affects which data cells a header cell applies to.\n> >\n> > Here is a markup fragment showing a table:\n> >\n> > &lt;table&gt;\n> > &lt;thead&gt;\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;th&gt; ID &lt;th&gt; Measurement &lt;th&gt; Average &lt;th&gt; Maximum\n> > &lt;tbody&gt;\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;th scope=rowgroup&gt; Cats &lt;td&gt; &lt;td&gt;\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; 93 &lt;th scope=row&gt; Legs &lt;td&gt; 3\\.5 &lt;td&gt; 4\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; 10 &lt;th scope=row&gt; Tails &lt;td&gt; 1 &lt;td&gt; 1\n> > &lt;tbody&gt;\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;th scope=rowgroup&gt; English speakers &lt;td&gt; &lt;td&gt;\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; 32 &lt;th scope=row&gt; Legs &lt;td&gt; 2\\.67 &lt;td&gt; 4\n> > &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; 35 &lt;th scope=row&gt; Tails &lt;td&gt; 0\\.33 &lt;td&gt; 1\n> > &lt;/table&gt;\n> >\n> > \n> >\n> > The headers in the first row all apply directly down to the rows in their column.\n> >\n> > The headers with the explicit scope attributes apply to all the cells in their row group other than the cells in the first column.\n> >\n> > The remaining headers apply just to the cells to the right of them.\n>\n> If my understanding of [the rules](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#header-and-data-cell-semantics) is correct, then either of the following fixes would be correct:\n>\n> - remove `scope=row` from the four `th` elements with that attribute, so that \"The remaining headers\" refers to them as originally intended.\n> - Change the description to reference the explicit scope values.\n>\n> I think the first option is at least slightly better since this example is specifically about the `rowgroup` scope and it would leave `rowgroup` as the only explicit scope value in the example.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7492/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 26, 2022, 5:28 PM UTC (d5c3178)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7492/80f4038...d5c3178/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 26, 2022, 5:28 PM UTC (d5c3178)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7492/tables.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 26, 2022, 5:28 PM UTC (d5c3178)\">/tables.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7492/80f4038...d5c3178/tables.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 26, 2022, 5:28 PM UTC (d5c3178)\">diff</a> )",
